X1
  where :
    X1 =  y = 2 + (1/10) * z


Applying substitution 
    y = 2 + (1/10) * z

   to    : 
    z + 4 * ((1/2) * (-6 * y + -1 * z)) + 3 * y = 1

   gives : 
    3 * ((1/10) * z) + 4 * ((1/2) * (-1 * z + -6 * ((1/10) * z))) + z = 19


Solving 3 * ((1/10) * z) + 4 * ((1/2) * (-1 * z + -6 * ((1/10) * z))) + z = 19 for z

Tidying to (3/10) * z + 4 * ((1/2) * ((-3/5) * z + -1 * z)) + z = 19

Polynomial -19 + 4 * ((1/2) * (-1 * z + (-3/5) * z)) + (3/10) * z + z becomes 

(-19/10) * z + -19 when in normal form

Answer is : 
X1
  where :
    X1 =  z = -10

Substituting back in y solution

Applying substitution 
    z = -10

   to    : 
    y = 2 + (1/10) * z

   gives : 
    y = 1

Substituting back in x solution

Applying substitution 
    z = -10
    y = 1

   to    : 
    x = (1/2) * (-1 * z + -6 * y)

   gives : 
    x = 2


Final Answers are : 
((X1 & X2) & X3)
  where :
    X1 =  z = -10
    X2 =  y = 1
    X3 =  x = 2

